WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.129
Digital fashion is real, and it exists
in so&nbsp;many virtual universes,

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:08.000
ranging from basic social networks 
to fully developed virtual worlds

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.130
known&nbsp;as the metaverse.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.734
Because of my gaming 
experience, I kept thinking:

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.471
“How and why could people
&nbsp;wear digital garments?” 

00:00:14.471 --> 00:00:16.669
This is when I started experimenting

00:00:16.669 --> 00:00:18.968
with what today we know as&nbsp;digital fashion.

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:23.083
With Carolina Herrera, we 
collaborated on a runway dress

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:24.642
and developed&nbsp;an app where you can

00:00:24.642 --> 00:00:27.530
wear the dress on your phone 
using augmented reality. 

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:30.017
And with Jean Paul&nbsp;Gaultier, 
we collaborated on

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:32.455
a piece that was part of
their couture collection. 

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:36.094
Fashion brands are&nbsp;selling 
authenticated digital fashion items

00:00:36.094 --> 00:00:38.432
that are usually sold out as 
soon as they are released.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.835
Balenciaga has collaborated with Fortnite,

00:00:40.835 --> 00:00:45.121
and Gucci bag was sold inside Roblox 
for more&nbsp;than its worth in real life.

00:00:45.742 --> 00:00:48.561
Fortnite itself has sold more than 
two billion worth of skins

00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:51.633
and game extras for in-game 
character dressing.

